.TH smi-docker-push "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Docker Command"
.SH NAME
smi-docker-push \- Push a built Docker image to the registry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-docker-push
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-docker-push
is the third step of the Docker build process of the toolset:
.BR smi-docker-prepare (1),
.BR smi-docker-build (1),
.BR smi-docker-push .
It sources the \fBdocker.sh\fR library and the \fBbuild.sh\fR script of the current directory, and
pushes the image that
.BR smi-docker-build (1)
built and tagged. Nothing is built here, so a push can be repeated, or left out for a local
build, without building again.
.PP
The steps are:
.IP 1.
\fBbuild_login\fR: \fBdocker login\fR, which uses stored credentials or asks for them.
.IP 2.
\fBbuild_push\fR: pushes the \fBlatest\fR tag, then the
\fIDOCKER_PROJECT_VERSION\fR tag, of
\fIDOCKER_ID_ORGANIZATION\fB/\fIDOCKER_PROJECT_NAME\fR.
.PP
Each step runs while the previous one succeeds.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Set by \fBbuild.sh\fR:
.TP
\fBDOCKER_ID_ORGANIZATION\fR
Docker registry organization or user.
.TP
\fBDOCKER_PROJECT_NAME\fR
Name of the image.
.TP
\fBDOCKER_PROJECT_VERSION\fR
Version tag of the image.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./build.sh
Sets the variables above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the last step that ran, so a failed login or push fails the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Build, check the image, then publish it:
.RS
.nf
smi-docker-prepare
smi-docker-build
docker run --rm example/app:latest --version
smi-docker-push
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
